# Integrations & CSV

## Marketplace adapters

- Use provider-specific adapter interfaces (Amazon, Flipkart, Shopify, etc.) behind a shared port; do not scatter provider logic in UI.
- Use authorized APIs and documented OAuth/token flows only.
- Never ask users for marketplace account passwords.
- Never claim a connection is live unless authentication and the relevant operations have been verified in this environment.
- Clearly distinguish **demo**, **imported**, and **synchronized** data in storage and UI.

## CSV import

- Validate headers, types, dates, currencies, and required fields before commit.
- Preview and validate rows; report counts: valid, invalid, skipped, duplicate.
- Support column mapping when marketplace exports differ.
- Apply file-size and row-count limits; reject oversized files safely.
- Make imports transactional where appropriate; handle partial failures without corrupting prior good data.
- Prevent duplicate transactions on repeated imports (stable external IDs + uniqueness).
- Preserve import provenance (source file, adapter, timestamp) and useful per-row error details.

## CSV export & reconciliation

- Protect against CSV formula injection on export (escape leading `=`, `+`, `-`, `@`).
- Never silently reconcile ambiguous financial transactions; record matching methods and audit manual changes.
